\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces First operationally selected candidate interval for each quantile level $\tau $ and signal-to-noise ratio. For compactness, write $T^\star = T_{\mathrm  {est}}$ and $k^\star = \setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle k$}\mathaccent "0362{k}(T^\star )$. The interval is selected by requiring it to contain $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle l$}\mathaccent "0362{l}(T^\star )$ and then minimizing its width over all admissible candidates. The last column reports $w_{k^\star }(T^\star ) = T_{\mathrm  {exit}}^{(k^\star )}(T^\star ) - T_{\mathrm  {entry}}^{(k^\star )}(T^\star )$.}}{19}{table.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:simulation_est_interval}{{3}{19}{First operationally selected candidate interval for each quantile level $\tau $ and signal-to-noise ratio. For compactness, write $T^\star = T_{\mathrm {est}}$ and $k^\star = \widehat k(T^\star )$. The interval is selected by requiring it to contain $\widehat l(T^\star )$ and then minimizing its width over all admissible candidates. The last column reports $w_{k^\star }(T^\star ) = T_{\mathrm {exit}}^{(k^\star )}(T^\star ) - T_{\mathrm {entry}}^{(k^\star )}(T^\star )$}{table.caption.14}{}}
